  "rakkhituṃ": "неопр. <i>[пер. ИИ]</i> To complete the task, I will translate the English definition of the Pali term \"rakkhituṃ\" into Russian following all given rules.\n\nThe Pali term is an infinitive verb. The English definition is \"to protect; to guard; to preserve\". These three meanings seem semantically distinct: \"protect\" implies shielding from harm, \"guard\" implies watching over or defending, and \"preserve\" implies maintaining or keeping intact. Since each is a different sense, I will provide three Russian translations.\n\nBracketed text: none in this definition.\n\nTranslate \"to protect\" as \"защищать\", \"to guard\" as \"охранять\", \"to preserve\" as \"сохранять\". These match the infinitive verb structure.\n\nNo idioms, proper nouns, or clarifications to retain.\n\nOutput only the translation, in one line, separated by `;`.\n\nResult: защищать; охранять; сохранять\n\nNo English remains, no extra labels, no comments.защищать; охранять; сохранять [√rakkh + ituṃ]",
